    <title>A made-up transient signal seen by two test detectors</title>
    <updated>2016-02-11T19:26:44Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1602.90837v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1602.90837v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Two invented detectors saw the same transient signal, with a peak strain of $1.0 \times 10^{-21}$, at a distance of $410^{+160}_{-180}$ Mpc and a redshift $z = 0.09^{+0.03}_{-0.04}$; the masses were $36^{+5}_{-4} M_\odot$ and $29^{+4}_{-4} M_\odot$. This abstract was written for Dispatch's tests and describes no real observation.</summary>
